Where surface-to-mask volume discrepancy is evaluated, the predefined
criterion is:

≤1.5% surface-to-mask volume discrepancy

provided that this criterion corresponds to the actually executed quality
control procedure.

Manuscript reporting of successful geometry QC requires corresponding
execution evidence.

If the underlying geometry-QC artifact is not recoverable, the criterion
remains a predefined QC specification rather than a verified historical
result.

