7. REFERENCE CONFIGURATION
======================================================================

End-diastolic geometry is designated as the primary reference configuration
unless the executed COMSOL model documents a different configuration.

End-systolic segmentation is retained as an anatomical and geometric
reference for the patient-specific reconstruction workflow.

The exact relationship between ED/ES geometry and the computational
reference state must follow the executed model implementation.

If the final COMSOL model uses only one phase as the computational reference,
the manuscript must report that configuration explicitly.

