======================================================================
10. BOUNDARY CONDITIONS
======================================================================

The model includes anatomically defined mechanical constraints required to
prevent nonphysical rigid-body motion while permitting physiological
deformation.

A basal mechanical constraint is included according to the implemented
model.

The exact basal spring/damper coefficients, if used, must be recovered from
the executed model or parameter registry.

The epicardial boundary is not to be assigned an additional displacement
constraint unless such a condition is explicitly present in the executed
model.

Boundary-condition definitions must remain anatomically and mechanically
consistent with the finite-element solid-mechanics formulation.

Statements such as:

"z-periodic boundary"
"y-periodic boundary"
"x-radiative boundary"

must NOT be included unless they are demonstrably implemented in the
executed COMSOL model.

