11. NUMERICAL SOLUTION
======================================================================

The finite-element equilibrium problem is solved using a geometrically
nonlinear formulation with Newton-type nonlinear iteration.

The exact solver settings must be obtained from the executed COMSOL model
or the authoritative solver configuration.

Potential controlled solver documentation includes:

- nonlinear solver type
- convergence tolerance
- relative tolerance
- absolute tolerance
- maximum iterations
- damping/line-search settings
- continuation settings
- stabilization settings, if any
- linear-solver configuration
- computational hardware
- COMSOL version.

Recovered documentation identifies Newton-type nonlinear solution as the
intended computational approach.

Exact solver tolerances remain subject to execution-evidence reconciliation.

