13. GRAVITY-RESPONSE NORMALIZATION
======================================================================

For normalized response analysis, the value at 1.00 g is used as the
reference denominator.

The normalized response is:

E_p(g) = value_at(g) / value_at(1.00 g) × 100

Thus:

1.00 g = 100% reference

This normalization must be applied consistently to all endpoints for which
normalized response is reported.

The direction of the gravity axis in the primary gravity-response figure
is:

1.00 g -> 0.75 g -> 0.50 g -> 0.38 g -> 0.16 g -> 0.00 g

representing decreasing gravitational loading from left to right.

