21. SENSITIVITY ANALYSIS
======================================================================

Sensitivity analysis is defined as a robustness assessment of the
gravity-dependent mechanical response.

Candidate perturbation domains include:

1. Fiber orientation
2. Passive material stiffness
3. Basal boundary-condition stiffness
4. Endocardial/cavity pressure.

Each perturbation should be evaluated relative to the reference model.

A general normalized change may be expressed as:

Delta Q (%) =
|Q_perturbed - Q_baseline| / |Q_baseline| × 100

Sensitivity results should be reported only if the corresponding
simulations are actually executed and the outputs are recoverable.

